Topi Linkala <nes@iki.fi> writes:
> Hello,
> 
> I've got a question on the vision system of vanilla NetHack 3.4.3.
> 
> In mkobj.c in function remove_object() which handles situation where
> ann object is removed from a floor position (after which it can enter
> almost anywhere).
> 
> There is a check for boulders: if an boulder is removed from a floor
> position then call unblock_point() for those coordinates. No checks if
> there are more boulders on the same spot.
> 
> I tried to check the vision system but got stumped. How is multiple
> boulder handled in this situation? Is it newsym() that keeps the
> location still blocked if there were two or more boulders?

Answer; they aren't. This is a bug.

(I tested in wizmode by setting up two boulders in the doorway to an
unvisited room while blindfolded, then letting a hostile storm giant
pick one up while I waited in the corridor outside:

        ----
     @H`...|
     #    .|
  #####
   #

You see that the room's been revealed even though one of the boulders
is still in place. I also didn't get a "The storm giant picks up a
boulder."  message to explain why the room was being revealed,
presumably because the square was still being handled as out of sight
at that point.)

